          </paramlist>
        </User>
        <Wire classid="WireOrthogonal" id="995184907" name="" x="540" y="180" w="64" h="64" orient="0" disable="false">
          <vertex x="0" y="0" />
          <vertex x="0" y="-54" />
          <vertex x="54" y="-54" />
        </Wire>
        <Sticky classid="Sticky" x="18" y="324" w="468" h="414" id="1779409513">
          <paramlist>
            <param name="font" value="1" />
            <param name="align" value="0" />
            <param name="style" value="1" />
            <param name="arrows" value="0" />
            <param name="fg_color" value="0" />
            <param name="bg_color" value="15792890" />
            <param name="full_font" value="Arial, 9.75pt" />
            <param name="opacity" value="25" />
            <param name="fg_color_adv" value="#FF000000" />
            <param name="bg_color_adv" value="#FFFAFAF0" />
            <param name="hl_color_adv" value="#FFFFFF00" />
            <param name="bdr_color_adv" value="#FF95918C" />
          </paramlist><![CDATA[~~~~~~~ INSTRUCTIONS ~~~~~~~~

--> See videos on our website!
  https://sites.google.com/view/pmview

First, copy the .pslx library file and .txt data files to your PSCAD case folder.  Open the case and library in PSCAD and paste the PMView block into your plant model and connect to the POI.  Disconnect the plant from any sources; the PMView block serves as an "infinite bus" source.  Use an integer to specify the test or use the multi-run block to cycle-through tests (recommend using an integer block for your first run).

Right-click the PMView block and set Delay, the time when the disturbance happens (PSCAD model must be fully initialized, for example use delay=5).  Double-click to go inside the PMView block and, for each of the three sub-blocks, right-click, Edit Parameters, and set the base voltage and frequency.  If running SCR, the SCR block has additional required settings.

If running via multi-run, you will only see the final plots.  Past plots are saved as files numbered per test profile r000x.  Use EnerPlot, Excel, or similar view tool.]]></Sticky>
        <Sticky classid="Sticky" x="18" y="18" w="378" h="288" id="1322283498">
          <paramlist>
            <param name="font" value="1" />
            <param name="align" value="0" />
            <param name="style" value="1" />
            <param name="arrows" value="0" />
            <param name="fg_color" value="0" />
            <param name="bg_color" value="15792890" />
            <param name="full_font" value="Tahoma, 9pt" />
            <param name="opacity" value="25" />
            <param name="fg_color_adv" value="#FF000000" />
            <param name="bg_color_adv" value="#FFFAFAF0" />
            <param name="hl_color_adv" value="#FFFFFF00" />
            <param name="bdr_color_adv" value="#FF95918C" />
          </paramlist><![CDATA[PMView - Version 2.3 - August 13, 2024

Jonathan Rose and Yunzhi Cheng
Jonathan.Rose@ercot.com, yunzhi.cheng@ercot.com

For updates, please see https://sites.google.com/view/pmview


THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.
]]></Sticky>
        <Sticky classid="Sticky" id="743950099" x="702" y="36" w="198" h="216" colors="0, 15792890">
          <paramlist>
            <param name="full_font" value="Tahoma, 9pt" />
            <param name="align" value="0" />
            <param name="style" value="1" />
            <param name="font" value="1" />
            <param name="fg_color" value="0" />
            <param name="bg_color" value="8454016" />
            <param name="arrows" value="4" />
            <param name="opacity" value="25" />
            <param name="fg_color_adv" value="#FF000000" />
            <param name="bg_color_adv" value="#FF80FF80" />
            <param name="hl_color_adv" value="#FFFFFF00" />
            <param name="bdr_color_adv" value="#FF95918C" />
          </paramlist><![CDATA[~~~~ Test Profile ~~~~~

You can use a Multiple Run block to cycle through each test in order, restarting PSCAD automatically, and saving a new .out file each time (enable .out saving in the case settings). It is recommended that the first time you run that you set the test_profile using a constant and not have the multi-run block in your case until everthing is working as expected.
]]></Sticky>
        <User classid="UserCmp" name="master:consti" id="506938233" x="648" y="72" w="76" h="22" z="-1" orient="4" defn="master:consti" link="-1" q="4" disable="false">
          <paramlist link="-1" name="" crc="74846674">
