        </User>
        <User classid="UserCmp" name="master:annotation" id="748181448" x="450" y="216" w="20" h="126" z="-1" orient="3" defn="master:annotation" link="-1" q="4" disable="false">
          <paramlist link="-1" name="" crc="5338603">
            <param name="AL1" value="Connect IBR POI here" />
            <param name="AL2" value="" />
          </paramlist>
        </User>
        <Sticky classid="Sticky" id="859263480" x="576" y="360" w="684" h="414" colors="0, 15792890">
          <paramlist>
            <param name="full_font" value="Tahoma, 9pt" />
            <param name="align" value="0" />
            <param name="style" value="1" />
            <param name="font" value="1" />
            <param name="fg_color" value="0" />
            <param name="bg_color" value="8454016" />
            <param name="arrows" value="0" />
            <param name="opacity" value="25" />
            <param name="fg_color_adv" value="#FF000000" />
            <param name="bg_color_adv" value="#FF80FF80" />
            <param name="hl_color_adv" value="#FFFFFF00" />
            <param name="bdr_color_adv" value="#FF95918C" />
          </paramlist><![CDATA[~~~~~~~~ CUSTOMIZING TESTS ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

The test profile can be customized by editing the corresponding .txt file:

1.  Flatstart
2.  LVRT		profile_LVRT.txt
3.  HVRT 		profile_HVRT.txt
4.  V-down 		profile_VDW.txt
5.  V-up 		profile_VUP.txt
6. LVRT(2800 piece)	2800_LVRT_WGR2.txt  (or)   2800_LVRT_PVGR2.txt
7. HVRT (2800)		2800_HVRT.txt
   Transient (if enabled):  See transient block within PMView
8. Angle down		profile_ADW.txt
9. Angle up		profile_AUP.txt
10. Custom fault(s)	(See interior block within PMview for settings)
11. Hz Down		profile_HzDW.txt
12. Hz Up		profile_HzUP.txt
13. V up and down	profile_VUP_DW.txt
14. SCR:  profile_SCR.txt  (See interior block within PMView for settings.)
15. PMU_playback	PMU_data.txt


Profile 6 uses either file depending on whether "Wind" (WGR) or "Solar" (PVGR) is selected in the PMView block parameter settings (right-click the yellow PMView block, edit parameters).]]></Sticky>
        <Sticky classid="Sticky" id="794677864" x="918" y="18" w="324" h="324" colors="0, 15792890">
          <paramlist>
            <param name="full_font" value="Tahoma, 9pt" />
            <param name="align" value="0" />
            <param name="style" value="1" />
            <param name="font" value="1" />
            <param name="fg_color" value="0" />
            <param name="bg_color" value="8454016" />
            <param name="arrows" value="0" />
            <param name="opacity" value="25" />
            <param name="fg_color_adv" value="#FF000000" />
            <param name="bg_color_adv" value="#FF80FF80" />
            <param name="hl_color_adv" value="#FFFFFF00" />
            <param name="bdr_color_adv" value="#FF95918C" />
          </paramlist><![CDATA[TEST PROFILES:
____________________
1.  Flatstart
2.  LVRT (data file has ERCOT Legacy)
3.  HVRT (data file has ERCOT Legacy)
4.  V-down
5.  V-up
6.  LVRT Dips (ieee2800 / nogrr245 Preferred)
7.  HVRT Preferred (ieee2800)
8.  Angle down
9.  Angle up
10.  Custom fault(s)
11.  Frequency Down
12.  Frequency Up
13.  V up and down w/ impedance
14.  Short Ckt Ratio SCR
15.  PMU playback

** All tests are customizable by the data files, see note below. **]]></Sticky>
        <Sticky classid="Sticky" id="661301026" x="1260" y="18" w="198" h="306" colors="0, 15792890">
          <paramlist>
            <param name="full_font" value="Tahoma, 9pt" />
            <param name="align" value="0" />
            <param name="style" value="1" />
            <param name="font" value="1" />
            <param name="fg_color" value="0" />
            <param name="bg_color" value="8454016" />
            <param name="arrows" value="0" />
            <param name="opacity" value="25" />
            <param name="fg_color_adv" value="#FF000000" />
            <param name="bg_color_adv" value="#FF80FF80" />
            <param name="hl_color_adv" value="#FFFFFF00" />
            <param name="bdr_color_adv" value="#FF95918C" />
          </paramlist><![CDATA[~~~ Voltage Support Test ~~~

All plants in ERCOT will need to undergo VSS testing.  You can modify the "V up and down" test to mirror the VSS testing to check maximum reactive capability and voltage regulation accuracy.  Nodal Operating Guide 2.7.3.5(4) requires plants to regulate their POIB voltage within a thight tolerance.  Follow the below link for a sample IRR VSS test:

https://www.ercot.com/files/docs/2020/12/30/IRR_AVR_testing_expectations_12302020.docx ]]></Sticky>
        <grouping />
      </schematic>
